<h2>What actually determines the price you're quoted</h2>
<p>We don't quote turmeric off a flat per-kilo rate, because the number moves on several genuinely independent factors. Curcumin content is the biggest single lever — a 5%+ extraction-grade lot costs meaningfully more to produce and source than standard 2.5% culinary-grade material, since higher-curcumin rhizomes are a smaller share of any harvest. Form matters too: whole finger and mother bulb (prized specifically for extraction) command different pricing than cut/split or powder, which carries additional processing cost. Beyond spec, the Erode and Nizamabad market auction cycle moves with each new harvest (January-March harvest, curing over the following weeks, so prices typically firm up before the new crop clears the market and ease once fresh stock is available), the size of that year's crop across Telangana, Andhra Pradesh and Tamil Nadu, and prevailing INR/AED exchange rates and Jebel Ali freight rates.</p>
<p>Quotes are issued FOB, CIF or CFR against your specific form, curcumin target, moisture tolerance, packaging and destination port — never as a generic per-tonne rate. To get an accurate quote fast, tell us: form (finger/split/powder), target curcumin %, intended end use (culinary vs. extraction/nutraceutical), packaging preference, quantity and destination port.</p>
